        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "EO 10634 authorizes Defense Production Act section 302 disaster loans for defense-required facilities, with the determination made by the Director of the Office of Defense Mobilization. The first held end is its express revocation by EO 12148 section 5-106, effective July 15, 1979 by that order's own words (signed July 20, 1979). Successor-office orders EO 10773, EO 11051 and EO 11725 redirect references or functions and are recorded as later events in the reason, not as ends. Searches: the U.S. Code and eCFR searches record two citation hits each for this order without a located text slice in the dossier, so they were not treated as evidence of continuation; the OFR disposition-note search lists the EO 12148 revocation.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"Checked for an earlier end: (1) the order has no sunset or condition ending it; (2) EO 10773, EO 11051 and EO 11725 change the responsible office but do not revoke or terminate the order, so they are later events and not ends; (3) no held source shows an earlier lapse of the Defense Production Act section 302 loan authority; (4) EO 12148 names EO 10634 and revokes it, effective July 15, 1979.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The loan authority itself is conferred by section 302 of the Defense Production Act of 1950, which the order invokes; that statute is independent of the order and is not held in the packet. The order adds only the direction that such loans may be made for major-disaster facilities determined by the Director to be required for national defense.\",\"savings_check\":\"EO 12148 contains no savings sentence for this revocation in the revocation provision; loans already made under the order would remain governed by their own terms and by the statute, but held evidence shows no continuing right or duty that arises only from the order, so none is recorded.\",\"scope_check\":\"One clause covers the whole order. EO 12148 revokes the order as amended and has no exception for it.\"}",
